    {
      "title": "Negotiate",
      "desc": "Agree on a version",
      "detail": "The laptop lists every SMB version it speaks, from 2.0.2 to 3.1.1, and says it requires signing. The NAS picks 3.1.1, the newest. Both sides keep a SHA-512 hash of everything exchanged from here until the login is done. It goes into the keys, so if anyone changed these messages on the way, to force an older version for instance, the login would fail.",
      "facts": [
