    {
      "title": "Close the File",
      "desc": "And keep 445 at home",
      "detail": "CLOSE hands the file ID back; the connection stays open for the next file. SMB 3 can also encrypt every message with AES-GCM, for one share or a whole server. Here only signing protects the messages, so anyone on the network could read the file as it passed. Port 445 should never be reachable from the internet: the WannaCry worm (2017) spread through a flaw in the old SMB1.",
